            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0182" n="66" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg66"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/1071.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The German Ambassador to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Imperial German Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: The Imperial Government
                    has instructed me to express to your excellency its special satisfaction at
                    finding the views concerning the American policy in the Far East, as set forth
                    in your excellency’s note of the 3d instant relative to China, to be in full
                    consonance with the German pursuits in China. Your excellency’s announcement
                    appears to be fully appreciated in Germany.</p>
                <p>Taking special pleasure in carrying out these instructions, I avail [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Bernstorff.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
